From: BaresipKit <baresipkit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:06:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] stream: restart the RTP timeout after hold

check_rtp_handler() only checks a stream while it is sendrecv, but the
time of the last received packet is not touched while the stream is on
hold. When a call is resumed after a hold longer than the RTP timeout,
the first check sees the gap of the whole hold and closes the call,
although the peer had no reason to send. A call held for 20 seconds,
resumed and held again would end with "no video RTP packets received
for 31350 milliseconds" moments after it was resumed.

Move the time of the last packet forward while the stream is not
sendrecv, so the timeout counts from the moment the stream is sendrecv
again. Streams that never received RTP are unchanged.
---
 src/stream.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/stream.c b/src/stream.c
index 2822a72..5af01c6 100644
--- a/src/stream.c
+++ b/src/stream.c
@@ -339,6 +339,8 @@ static void check_rtp_handler(void *arg)
 		}
 	}
 	else {
+		rtprecv_set_ts_last(strm->rx, now);
+
 		debug("check_rtp: not checking \"%s\" RTP (dir=%s)\n",
 			  sdp_media_name(strm->sdp),
 			  sdp_dir_name(sdp_media_dir(strm->sdp)));
